{"title":"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems\">2020 AMC 12A #5</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems\">2020 AMC 10A #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d7701e9469f26e22c106341791344b28f3196443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e395ecfa661165ea0d06fc0114eb7c24f075ead7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> inclusive, can be arranged to form a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-by-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> square in which the sum of the numbers in each row, the sum of the numbers in each column, and the sum of the numbers along each of the main diagonals are all the same. What is the value of this common sum?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7567d9da241f4573816f70f4fe7167d1fd903f93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 5\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 10\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 25\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"380\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without loss of generality, consider the five rows in the square. Each row must have the same sum of numbers, meaning that the sum of all the numbers in the square divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the total value per row. The sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc97a414da20dbc661d32d60472aa7aaff0bbd86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10+-9+...+14=11+12+13+14=50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"363\" height=\"15\" />, and the common sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e3846b65c25c8d69c9143aabb500064532c96af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{5}=\\boxed{\\text{(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take the sum of the middle 5 values of the set (they will turn out to be the mean of each row). We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d103ff29de4cec8d47b20fff89ddd997379bc3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"223\" height=\"28\" /> as our answer.\n~Baolan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Taking the average of the first and last terms, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d7701e9469f26e22c106341791344b28f3196443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we have that the mean of the set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There are 5 values in each row, column or diagonal, so the value of the common sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faf66240ecba6fcb8c48d56281ea7bb1933fa46e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot2$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5f6002355beb793dc42eb5090d34ffef7aceda6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />. \n~Arctic_Bunny, edited by KINGLOGIC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us consider the horizontal rows.  Since there are five of them, each with constant sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we can add up the 25 numbers in 5 rows for a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />.  Since the sum of the 25 numbers used is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3541f7c3e3c0ab5edcb7ab9f9895449e70f9978d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10-9-8-\\cdots{}+12+13+14+15=11+12+13+14+15=50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"549\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac354f37aa0664e7292e65c231d994425dacd3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x=50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076a6145b447a11b81b6a0c32393c781656f7870.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" />. \n~cw357\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The mean of the set of numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/166b64245de54cabb15fa6a9bc1ab4407835d7d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(14-10) \\div 2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />. The numbers around it must be equal (i.e. if the mean of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a98cc52a4ceef5de20a62e2be2e7d5bb5bf77df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+4=1+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />.)\nOne row of the square would be \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/3/de3091fc4d9d5f46c0717e31bb904441d5d96769.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\square  \\square  2  \\square  \\square\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Adding the numbers would be \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb80231ddaf31a166523ada64db3e0709900ee32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0, 1, 2, 3, 4\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>with a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bd710c9221212dba3bf44ccb7d478426ac3ac8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the sum of each row, column, and diagonal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then we have a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/38588fafb659d83dc4c41024358d54ce788611d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> for the sum. The sum of the rows and columns is the sum of all the numbers doubled, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/50725d02272a2fda9ca7e1b8c616b9ddda84ce74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\cdot2=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f1e631c7e57835a403fffdbbd850eba7ee0fae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100+2x=12x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea19ba4464f4fba89dbf7b0a8e531b053ec2d02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100=10x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53baa4be927ee9f877ebc4ec49981437d583812e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />.\n~MC413551\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A cool thing to find is that with magic squares, the smallest and largest number are either in the same row, column and diagonal to balance the equation out. To continue doing this, the other numbers in that same line form an arithmetic sequence. With our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> term generally being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and our last term being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb412b4622f8ab98c3f9041752028b25b8e70794.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />, by working out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/697e1e1c912ac56d3946fd44f3408e3d5423587b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+(n-1)d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" /> formula. For a 5 by 5, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d5cea31c66ebe6e26b3a41f6c64316f0f618b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 6$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. To apply this we start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d7701e9469f26e22c106341791344b28f3196443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" />, and our last term being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We increase by increments by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get the 5 numbers in our line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbba2ad26e0ce11e1d4425a0e882bb2a6d6bf15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10, -4, 2, 8, 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />. This adds up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bd710c9221212dba3bf44ccb7d478426ac3ac8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>(Note the goal of this solution was just to point out something I found that I thought was cool, I don't advise using it in actual competitions)\n</p><p>-CubiksRube\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can solve this by counting how many times each square is included when summing all possible lines. The number of possible lines that can be drawn is 12 (5 rows + 5 columns + 2 main diagonals).\n</p><p>First, the sum of all 25 integers in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/6/1b61462eebb18949776367cc8923f577cfae1c3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{-10, -9, \\dots, 14\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the common sum of a single line. The sum of all 12 lines combined is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/5368830010090f55728f58899146dbd9ae8b17af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>However, not all squares are used an equal amount of times in these 12 lines. Let's categorize them:\n</p>\n<ul><li>The center square is used in 4 lines. Let its value be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.</li>\n<li>The remaining 8 squares on the main diagonals are used in 3 lines each. Let the sum of these 8 squares be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>The remaining 16 squares are used in 2 lines each. Let the sum of these 16 squares be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>We can set up a system of equations based on this information:\n</p><p>1. The sum of all squares is 50:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/31819a5f5f410ee37c71f80397a76840a834162a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + b + c = 50\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n2. The sum of all 12 lines counts each square multiple times based on its position:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d9b6a1ec376fbb7acdda5b144a62ef139119ebf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12S = 4a + 3b + 2c\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4f4d47e70fba0259672139cd9b473b99e7ab80c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a + 3b + 2c \\equiv 0 \\pmod{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We just need to find a combination of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is a factor of 50, and then scale it up.\nA simple combination that works is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cefa6855d2216036df094012f7ad2a7e4e204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d65baaf9671227780dd04ab952911036aa5c868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/8271d4342b38d2ab38bb626ffad8b9dae00b5e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. The sum here is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2931c4be7df790e21874687b8529b7a5b2dd30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + 2 + 3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />.\nSince we need the sum to be 50, we can multiply our combination by 10 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cefa6855d2216036df094012f7ad2a7e4e204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/5125cb334346579f5246540b9d1cbede37bb37d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=20$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05c6c0f8a442fd01f2ef4bfe13c07e44bfdbbda2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. (Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbdac0016addc857bc7db299691e9be9df569634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + 20 + 30 = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" />, satisfying our first equation).\n</p><p>Now, plug this combination back into our line sum equation:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/964139e6ca16ce1bf6e3fcb20248d96be78dd47f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12S = 4(0) + 3(20) + 2(30)\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31af5e15ab586b6164a3ab3eda7e5c87bd268671.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12S = 0 + 60 + 60\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349db2e4f564bba7487648a46979e581746eaab2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12S = 120\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f109a22f72ec0153473803ce7030c6342c0faf8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = 10\\]\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>The common sum is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5f6002355beb793dc42eb5090d34ffef7aceda6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>-PandaGod7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Zf4HCY-y5Z4\">https://youtu.be/Zf4HCY-y5Z4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/JEjib74EmiY\">https://youtu.be/JEjib74EmiY</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n[starts from 1.08 in the video]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PHHBIiIlCY0\">https://youtu.be/PHHBIiIlCY0</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 4 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mgEZOXgIZXs?t=1\">https://youtu.be/mgEZOXgIZXs?t=1</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A\">2020 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A\">2020 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofpr